      "writtenOn": "2022-08-30T17:58:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sbc decoder does the find syncword also. https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/embdrv/sbc/decoder/srce/decoder-sbc.c;drc\u003d01a8f0414c3c28071d24f0f086a05e6f14d24bab;l\u003d281\n\nSo, by skipping the h1 header, the behavior remains the same.\n\nWe have 58 instead of 57 because of the padding 0 in the end that the mSBC decoder actually check and reflect on the `oi_size`.\n```\n  /* mSBC is designed with 8 bits of zeros at the end for padding. */\n  if (context-\u003emSbcEnabled) {\n    *frameBytes -\u003d 1;\n  }\n```\n\nRemove the logic in decoder-sbc.c and change to pass 57, considering we don\u0027t really care if the padding byte is 0 or not, which makes the logic meaningless.",
      "parentUuid": "d00bb06a_187b547f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "e9bed4e2ba2a9867da181044f76203c66327d168",
